# The injected fault, testing=UnderstateEffects, is a single fault that applies in two places. The walk removes the named effect from the effects of an operation.
# So does escape analysis, which computes the effects again for what is known about a fresh object.
# Here Link's summary of bump() is treated as if it listed no write of ObjectFields, so the field of the fresh box is read as the constructor left it.
# While escape analysis still used the complete effects entry, the fault changed nothing here, and every control on a fresh object was vacuous.
# f1 = bump
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# CHECK: sum 20.
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(LIE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=UnderstateEffects:Callee/f1/ObjectFields
# LIE: sum 2.
# LIE-NEXT: exited with 0
